ing partisanship.", "watch": "The first general-election polls in Delaware, or a decisive shift in the national political environment, could move this forecast toward or away from a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Delaware enters the 2028 presidential race as a Democratic-leaning state, with a partisan lean of roughly eight points toward Democrats and no incumbent on the ballot after the term-limited Republican presidency. The state has consistently sided with Democratic presidential candidates in recent cycles, and nothing in the current evidence points to a competitive general election here.\n\nNo state polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market prices are yet available for this race, and recent headlines focus on the national Democratic primary field rather than the Delaware general election. The forecast therefore rests on the state's underlying partisanship, pointing to a Democratic win with a margin near eight points. Uncertainty is wider than usual because the 2028 national environment is unknown, but a Republican upset would require a substantial national shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8204, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7838, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7798, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7761, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7732, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8108, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7706, "margin": 8.0}]}